SPEC = {
 "file":"cover_frontier_health_deployment_strategist",
 "label":"Frontier Health Deployment Strategist",
 "paras":[
 r"I am writing to apply for the Deployment Strategist position at Frontier Health. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have worked on healthcare AI with clinicians and clients, and on getting tools that I built actually adopted by the people meant to use them. I am particularly interested in this role because it sits exactly where those two things meet: taking AI into a healthcare organisation and making sure it is live, safe and used.",

 r"What attracts me most to Frontier Health is that the product is aimed at the administrative work that clinical care quietly depends on, and that you deploy into the teams, processes and tools already in place rather than asking them to start again. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved. The part of the role I find most compelling is owning the outcome after the contract is signed, because that is where most technology in healthcare succeeds or quietly stalls.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and operations data in SQL and Python and build KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. I also built an AI agent using Claude Code that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, and it is now used by my own team and by partner teams. The hardest part was not building it. It was understanding the existing process, deciding which steps the agent should own and which still needed a person, and then supporting colleagues as they changed how they worked. That is a small version of what a deployment is.",

 r"My closest experience to this role is DS Digital Technology, where I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing medical AI engagement for a pharmaceutical client. I worked with clinical experts to define what a safe answer looks like, including red-line rules for answers that must never be given, and designed a 246-question benchmark and six-dimension safety rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard for evaluating the AI. I built the pipeline that scored more than 2,400 responses, ran blinded comparisons, and presented the findings to clinical and business stakeholders, including where the system was not yet ready. Turning clinical safety from a principle into a test that people can agree on is close to how I would approach the clinical safety step of a deployment.",

 r"At Ipsos Strategy3 I analysed more than 80 interviews with healthcare professionals and turned them into structured evidence and recommendations for client stakeholders, which taught me how much of the real work in healthcare happens in processes that nobody has written down. My MSc dissertation used 458,840 UK Biobank participants and is delivered as a deployed application, so I am used to the gap between a model working and a tool being usable.",

 r"I should be clear about some gaps. I have not yet led an NHS deployment, I have no hands-on experience of information governance or clinical safety standards such as DCB0129 and DCB0160, and I have not run a procurement process. These are the parts I would be learning on the job, alongside people who have done them many times.",

 r"I would bring Frontier Health real experience of healthcare AI and clinical safety evaluation, the ability to understand data and workflows quickly, comfort working with clinicians, operators and executives, and a habit of owning a problem until it is solved. I am happy to work from your Farringdon office or on customer sites five days a week. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029, after which I would need sponsorship.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience in healthcare AI and stakeholder delivery could help Frontier Health's customers reach live, adopted deployments.",
 ]
}
